REM's normout (norm_4) does not go into the elements of an AC term: it
gives k(a u b u b) => a u b u b, the b left (status 0, result
a u b u b). elanc-go goes into AC terms under normout as into the
arguments of a free operator (S7d plan, Task 6 ruling): a u c u c, as
normin (normin_ac, equal to REM).
